# Project Structure

SwiftDune is a Swift reimplementation of the 1992 Dune game by Cryo Interactive. It is organized into three main modules:

## Editor/
macOS SwiftUI app for viewing and inspecting original Dune game assets (sprites, fonts, sceneries, videos, globe, text).
- `EditorView.swift` / `EditorViewModel.swift` — main editor UI and state
- `Views/` — detail and list views for each asset type (sprites, scenery, fonts, video, globe, text)

## Engine/
Core engine shared by both Editor and Game. Handles audio, graphics, input, rendering, and resource decoding.
- `Audio/` — audio playback (`AudioPlayer`), Creative Voice format (`CreativeVoice`), HERAD music driver, OPL3 FM synthesis (`OPL3/`)
- `Graphics/` — pixel buffer, palette management, visual effects, drawing primitives
- `Input/` — keyboard and mouse handling
- `Rendering/` — Metal renderer and shaders
- `Resources/` — decoders for original game formats: sprites, fonts, scenery, globe, music, sound, video, sentences
- `DuneEngine.swift` — engine entry point
- `Node.swift` / `Animation.swift` — scene graph and animation system

## Game/
macOS SwiftUI app that runs the actual Dune game.
- `Scenes/` — individual game scenes (Intro, Prologue, Flight, Palace, Sietch, Credits, etc.)
- `UI/` — in-game UI elements
- `GameView.swift` / `GameViewModel.swift` — main game view and state
